---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Read Aura Living LLC's Privacy Policy covering personal information, communications, and SMS messaging." path="/privacy-policy/">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy Policy" title="Your information, handled with care." intro="Aura Living LLC respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you share with us." />
  <section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><article class="content-copy">
    <p><strong>Last Updated: November 23, 2026</strong></p>
    <p>Aura Living LLC ("Aura Living," "we," "our," or "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you share with us. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website (https://auralivingva.com/), apply for a rental property, reside in one of our managed communities, or communicate with us via phone, email, or SMS/text messaging.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>As a residential and commercial property management company, we collect information necessary to evaluate rental applications, manage leases, maintain properties, and communicate with prospective and current residents, property owners, and vendors.</p>
    <h3>Contact &amp; Identification Information</h3>
    <p>Full name, email address, phone number (including mobile numbers), mailing address, date of birth, government-issued identification, and Social Security Number (solely for background and credit screening).</p>
    <h3>Application &amp; Tenancy Information</h3>
    <p>Employment history, income verification, rental history, emergency contacts, vehicle information, pet information, and lease agreements.</p>
    <h3>Financial &amp; Payment Information</h3>
    <p>Bank account details, payment card information, rent payment history, and security deposit records (processed securely through third-party payment processors).</p>
    <h3>Maintenance &amp; Property Records</h3>
    <p>Work order requests, communication logs, and property access records.</p>
    <h3>Technical &amp; Website Usage Data</h3>
    <p>IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, and pages visited on our website, collected via cookies and similar tracking technologies.</p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information we collect for legitimate business and property management purposes, including to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Process rental applications, verify income, and conduct tenant screening (credit, background, and eviction checks) in compliance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</li>
      <li>Execute, administer, and enforce lease agreements and property management contracts.</li>
      <li>Process rent payments, security deposits, and utility billing.</li>
      <li>Coordinate property maintenance, repairs, inspections, and emergency services.</li>
      <li>Send service-related communications, including appointment reminders, maintenance updates, lease renewal notices, and account alerts via email, phone, or SMS.</li>
      <li>Respond to inquiries, tour requests, and customer support tickets.</li>
      <li>Comply with federal, state (including Virginia housing and consumer protection laws), and local housing laws, legal obligations, and regulatory requirements.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. SMS / Text Messaging &amp; 10DLC Compliance</h2>
    <p>Aura Living LLC utilizes SMS/text messaging (10-Digit Long Code / 10DLC) to communicate efficiently with prospective tenants, current residents, property owners, and vendors.</p>
    <h3>A. Consent &amp; Opt-In</h3>
    <p>By providing your mobile phone number through our website contact forms, rental portals, tour scheduling tools, or paper applications, and checking the designated SMS consent box, you expressly consent to receive text messages from Aura Living LLC. These messages may include tour confirmations, application status updates, maintenance notifications, rent reminders, and property alerts. Consent to receive SMS messages is not a condition of purchasing any goods, applying for housing, or entering into a lease agreement.</p>
    <h3>B. Message Frequency &amp; Rates</h3>
    <p>Message frequency varies based on your interactions with us (e.g., active maintenance requests, scheduled tours, or account activity). Message and data rates may apply depending on your mobile carrier plan. Check with your wireless provider for details.</p>
    <h3>C. Opt-Out &amp; Help Instructions</h3>
    <p>You may opt out of receiving SMS messages from us at any time: Reply STOP, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, or QUIT to any text message you receive from us. You will receive one final confirmation message verifying that you have been unsubscribed, and no further messages will be sent unless you opt back in. For assistance, reply HELP to any message, or contact us directly via email or phone using the details in Section 10.</p>
    <h3>D. Strict Prohibition on Third-Party Sharing (10DLC Carrier Requirement)</h3>
    <p>No mobile information, SMS opt-in data, or phone numbers collected for SMS/text messaging purposes will be shared, sold, rented, or disclosed to third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Information sharing with subcontractors in support services—such as customer service platforms or SMS gateway providers—is permitted solely to deliver the messaging service and is strictly prohibited from any secondary marketing use.</p>

    <h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
    <p>Except as strictly restricted in Section 3(D) regarding mobile and SMS opt-in data, we may share your personal information only in the following circumstances:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Property Owners &amp; Landlords:</strong> If we manage a property on behalf of a third-party owner, we share relevant tenancy, maintenance, and financial reporting data with that owner.</li>
      <li><strong>Service Providers &amp; Vendors:</strong> We share limited, necessary information with trusted third parties who perform services on our behalf, such as tenant screening agencies, payment processors, maintenance contractors, software providers (e.g., property management portals), and SMS delivery platforms. These parties are contractually obligated to protect your data and use it only for the services requested.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal &amp; Safety Compliance:</strong> We may disclose information when required by law, subpoena, court order, or government regulation, or when necessary to protect the rights, property, or safety of Aura Living LLC, our residents, or the public.</li>
      <li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of company assets, personal information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to the commitments made in this Privacy Policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>

    <h2>5. Data Security &amp; Retention</h2>
    <p>We implement administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect your personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. Sensitive data, such as Social Security Numbers and payment credentials, is encrypted in transit and at rest. While no method of electronic transmission or storage is 100% secure, we maintain industry-standard security protocols.</p>
    <p>We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this policy, comply with statutory recordkeeping obligations (such as tax, accounting, and fair housing laws), resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements.</p>

    <h2>6. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>Our website uses cookies and similar analytics tools to improve site functionality, remember user preferences, and analyze website traffic. You can control or disable cookies through your browser settings; however, disabling certain cookies may limit your ability to use features of our online resident or applicant portals.</p>

    <h2>7. U.S. State &amp; Virginia Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>Residents of Virginia (under the Virginia Consumer Data Protection Act - VCDPA) and other applicable U.S. states have specific rights regarding their personal data, including the right to access, correct, delete, portability, opt out of targeted advertising/sale/profiling, and non-discrimination. Aura Living LLC does not sell personal data or use it for targeted advertising. To exercise rights, contact Aura Living LLC using the contact details below; identity verification may be required. If a request is denied, an appeal may be submitted with “Appeal” in the subject line.</p>

    <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our website and services are not directed to individuals under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13 without verifiable parental or legal guardian consent (such as listing minor occupants on a household lease application). If we learn we have inadvertently collected personal information from a child under 13 outside of household lease documentation, we will delete it promptly.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised Last Updated date.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
    <p><strong>Aura Living LLC</strong><br />
      Mailing Address: {site.address}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
      Phone: <a href="tel:+17038284040">{site.phone}</a><br />
      Website: <a href={site.url}>{site.url}/</a>
    </p>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><h2>Questions about privacy?</h2><p>Contact Aura Living LLC using the email or phone number listed in Section 10.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact Aura Living LLC</a></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
